# Contact modal delivery: a form-relay endpoint (Formspree, Web3Forms, ...).
# Copy to .env.local and fill in. For the deployed site, set the same values in the
# repository settings (Settings > Secrets and variables > Actions): VITE_CONTACT_ENDPOINT
# as a variable, VITE_CONTACT_ACCESS_KEY as a secret. The deploy workflow passes them to the build.
#
# Without VITE_CONTACT_ENDPOINT the modal does not send anything itself: it opens the
# visitor's email app with the message ready (attachments are not offered then).
VITE_CONTACT_ENDPOINT=
# Only for services that need a key in the body (e.g. Web3Forms).
# NOTE: anything starting with VITE_ ends up in the public JavaScript, so this key is
# not secret. Protect the form where it is received instead: in the service's settings,
# restrict it to your domain and turn on its spam filter / captcha (hCaptcha or Turnstile).
VITE_CONTACT_ACCESS_KEY=
# Set to true only if your plan accepts file attachments (the free plans of Web3Forms and Formspree do not).
VITE_CONTACT_ATTACHMENTS=
